# OPERATIONS §2.3 (M3): load's last check (a literal key at a literal stepped range, L §2.5, §8.4) on a reality with
# scenarios. The base of L8_4_load_sees_literal_key with its def w's key fixed; the scenario s writes the bad literal
# in a def of its own, so s doesn't load and only s is refused (L §6.4, §8): its line, exit 1. (run makes this check
# when an ask in s is answered, and prints it on that ask; refcore's run has no other point at which to make it.)
=== options check exit=1
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input r[d in 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 days]: int

def w: int = r[2026-01-08]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r[*] = 0 "s"

ask q: w
=== s.tally
scenario s over t
  tally 2
  from 2026-06-01

def w2: int = r[2026-01-09]

ask q2: w2 in s
=== expect
scenario s: refused: LOAD-KEY 2026-01-09 is not a value of 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 day ...
